	"equipment": [
		{
			"id": "ePtso7YevzUYFOIyM",
			"description": "Power Armour, Plague-Fused",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 6: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 6 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nThe wearer's Nurgle's Gift natural DR adds on top of the armour DR listed here. Seals are rotted and leak: Weak Points 6. The suit cannot be taken off; it has grown into the body.\n\nLore: Death Guard plate has rusted, blistered and in places fused with the flesh beneath it, weeping fluids and crawling with vermin. The Plague Marines wear it as a gift from Nurgle, not as damage (Black Library Death Guard fiction, and the Horus Heresy novel Mortis for the Legion's fall).\n\nDesign: Mark IV heretic DR (torso 95, arms and legs 83, neck 58, face 70, eye 71, hand 58, foot 70), servo ST, weight and cost, included from the loyalist Mark IV entry. Weak Points 6 as for any traitor Mark IV. The Plague Marine's Nurgle's Gift (fused rotting flesh DR 10, Injury Tolerance) is a trait and adds on top of the armour; it is not counted here, so nothing is added twice.",
			"tags": [
				"Body Armor",
				"Chaos",
				"Heretic Astartes",
				"Nurgle",
				"Death Guard"
			],
			"tech_level": "11",
